narrative:
## Nesting Structs Inside Structs

Struct fields can hold any type — including other structs. This lets you build complex data from simple pieces.

### Defining Nested Structs

```xiom
type Address = {
  street: Str;
  city: Str;
}

type Person = {
  name: Str;
  home: Address;
}
```

First define `Address`, then use it as a field type in `Person`.

### Creating Nested Values

```xiom
let addr = Address{ street: "123 Main St"; city: "Springfield"; };
let person = Person{ name: "Alice"; home: addr; };
```

Or inline:

```xiom
let person = Person{
  name: "Bob";
  home: Address{ street: "456 Oak Ave"; city: "Rivertown"; };
};
```

### Accessing Nested Fields

Use dot notation to drill down:

```xiom
person.name;        // "Bob"
person.home.city;   // "Rivertown"
person.home.street; // "456 Oak Ave"
```

### Why Nesting?

Nesting groups related sub-data together. Instead of `person_street` and `person_city`, you have `person.home.street` — the structure mirrors reality.

